#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""jsw: run one target of a JS reverse-engineering benchmark with a worker model
in a sandbox container (see bench/jsvm1/HARNESS.md).

    jsw setup                      create or refresh the dsh profile `js-worker`
    jsw doctor                     check dsh, the profile, the image and which
                                   tools dsh offers the model
    jsw run --target tN [--model ID] [--effort low|high|max] [--timeout SECONDS]
            [--max-calls N] [--bench DIR]
    jsw resume RUN_ID [--prompt TEXT] [--timeout SECONDS]
    jsw merge RUN_ID... -o DIR [--force]
    jsw gc [--dry-run]             remove containers left by runs that died

`jsw run` stages the target into tmp/jsw-runs/<run-id>/, starts a container
(no network, read-only root, only public/ and work/ mounted), runs dsh with the
js-worker profile whose only tools are jsre_mcp.py's, then exports
work/submission/ to <run>/submission/, audits the tool log, removes the
container and prints summary.json. Exit 0: the worker finished and the audit
is clean; 1: the worker did not finish (timeout, error); 2: the run could not
start; 3: the audit found something that should have been impossible.
"""

